{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jynsxrhw7pmnodsebchamo6t3kd62xfqtg2mcgm73p6tgugnqbja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Result: the translation is correct — no divergence found\n\nThe library is small: one public function, `void driver(int x)`, which `memcpy`s the 4 bytes of `x` and prints them as lowercase hex via `printf(\"%02x\")` plus a newline.\n\n**Phase A** — artifacts created in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`.\n- Symbol parity was already exact: C exports exactly `driver`; so does Rust. Nothing was missing, so no module needed translating and no stub was added.\n- `print_hex` is `static` in C, so it's correctly *absent* from both ABIs — exporting it would itself be a divergence, which I test for.\n- `ERRORS.md` is empty **by derivation, not omission**: grep confirms the C has zero `return` statements, no asserts, no null/range checks, no error enum. The only conditional in the whole library is the `i < len` loop bound. Every `int` bit pattern is a valid input, so all coverage belongs in `CONFIGS.md`. Null-pointer and out-of-range-enum boundaries are documented N/A with reasons grounded in the signature (`driver` takes no pointer and no enum).\n\n**Phases B–D** — 15 tests pass in both `debug` and `release`, ~5,400 differential comparisons by default plus **210,000** in the extended sweep, all byte-identical. Both `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and called only through `dlsym`, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test. `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so the feature cross-product is genuinely one configuration — the runner verifies this by parsing `Cargo.toml` rather than assuming it.\n\n**Two harness bugs I found and fixed — worth flagging, since either would have made this report meaningless:**\n\n1. **Silent stale-artifact testing.** `cargo test` does *not* build the cdylib for `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, so my path fallback loaded an *older* `libdriver.so`. My first mutation test (flipping to `to_be_bytes`) **passed** — which is how I caught it. Every test up to that point had been validating a stale binary. Fixed with `assert_so_is_fresh`, which aborts loudly if the `.so` predates any source file.\n2. **fd 1 never restored on panic.** A panic inside the capture window left fd 1 pointing at the unlinked temp file, silently swallowing all later output *including the panic message explaining the failure*. Fixed with a `Drop` guard, plus library init hoisted before the redirect.\n\nI then **mutation-tested** the suite to prove it can fail: four injected bugs (byte order, `%x` vs `%02x`, dropped newline, wrong length) each produced 12 failing tests. `src/lib.rs` was restored afterwards and verified byte-identical to the original; `c_src/` sources are unmodified (only the instructed `build/` directory was added).\n\nTwo notes on things I changed beyond tests: I added `translation/.cargo/config.toml` setting `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1`, because fd-1 redirection is process-wide and concurrent tests corrupt each other's captures. Use `./run_tests.sh` rather than a bare `cargo test` — the latter can run against a stale `.so` (it will now abort rather than mislead you). Dependencies resolved from the local cargo cache with `--offline`, as network egress is blocked."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3912,"cache_read_input_tokens":76262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3912,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94d006a4-144a-4b93-92b8-cd627db296b7","uuid":"8506d5bd-b022-45f3-8230-ca1355388eb0","timestamp":"2026-08-28T16:24:02.945Z"}
